{% case_body "I built it." %}
  <p>A web app that lives on my phone like a native one. New plan arrives, I upload the <strong>PDF or CSV</strong>, it splits the weeks into days. Then it gets out of the way.</p>
  <p>Most gym apps feel like they were built by someone who's <em>never used one</em>. Too rigid. Supersets buried. So I built every flexibility I've ever missed:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Drop sets, supersets, rest-pause</strong> as first-class, not workarounds</li>
    <li><strong>Edit anything mid-session</strong>: reps, weight, swap an exercise</li>
    <li><strong>Last time's number</strong> right there on the row</li>
    <li><strong>Big numbers</strong>, readable mid-set</li>
    <li><strong>Plate stacking</strong>: tap each plate as you load the bar</li>
  </ul>
{% endcase_body %}

